  "query_preview": "../Wednesday through Friday/...The start of the period\nbegins with a relative lull in the weather on Wednesday with just\nscattered showers that should generally decrease in coverage by \nWednesday night. On Thursday, a low pressure system in the \nsoutheast Gulf of Alaska will be advancing northeast toward the \narea. There is still some model disagreement on the timing, track,\nand intensity of this system, although it does appear \nincreasingly likely that at least the southern third of the region\nwill have some impacts by midday Thursday into Friday. \nPrecipitation could still ultimately push north and affect much of\nthe panhandle, but that is not yet a certainty. Locally heavy \nrainfall and gusty winds are possible, with the heaviest rainfall \nover southern sections. We should see improving conditions by \nFriday night as high pressure builds into the Gulf.",
